      "content": "It's not safe to treat someone's diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) at home. DKA is a potentially life-threatening complication of diabetes that requires immediate medical treatment. Administering insulin alone without treating the underlying metabolic abnormalities, such as severe ketonemia and electrolyte imbalances, can lead to serious complications or even be fatal. Delaying emergency medical care could lead to worsening of the condition. Please take your partner to the emergency room right away. Their life might depend on it. Remember, no potential risks are worth experimenting with. Get them to a hospital immediately.",
